WEBVTT

00:00:09,970 --> 00:00:23,970
Last week when asked you recommended continuing IV vitamin C durian radio chemotherapy, but when would you do IV vitamin C infusion so that the vitamin C does not neutralize the effects of the days of treatment.

00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:37,970
So I would, you know, if, if the chemotherapy, you're only doing it for those five days of radiation, I would wait until after the radiation to do an IV infusion.

00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:42,970
Can you do liposomal vitamin C during that time?

00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:57,600
Well, again, there's different theories about this. Some practitioners would say, absolutely, you shouldn't be doing it every day. That'll help protect your healthy cells during the radiation.

00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:02,600
It's hard to argue with that, that that being a strong possibility.

00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:10,600
But you want that radiation to work as best as possible. So it was me, I'd probably wait.

00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:19,600
Even with the liposomal vitamin C until after I was done with those five days, it's not like 30 days that you're waiting on this.

00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:29,600
If I was doing a 30 day session of radiation, which isn't uncommon with a lot of people with cancer, then I would probably stay on the liposomal vitamin C.

00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:37,600
But for five days, I think I would go off of it. And then maybe wait another day or so afterwards and then go back on it.

